{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q409270","formula":"Cu₁₃VSn₃S₁₆","hill":"Cu13S16Sn3V","elements":["S","V","Cu","Sn"],"composition":{"S":16.0,"V":1.0,"Cu":13.0,"Sn":3.0},"names":{"en":"Nekrasovite"},"descriptions":{"en":"See Nekrasov Cossacks for another meaning Nekrasovite is a rare copper vanadium sulfosalt mineral with formula Cu26V2(Sn,As,Sb)6S32. It crystallizes in the isometric system and occurs as small grains in ore aggregates. It is a brown opaque metallic mineral with Mohs hardness of 4.5 and a specific gravity of 4.62."},"fame":9,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q409270","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nekrasovite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"photo","name":"Wikimedia Commons","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nekrasovite.jpg","license":"CC BY 4.0"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q1792933","formula":"Cu₃SnS₄","names":{"en":"Kuramite"},"elements":["S","Cu","Sn"],"fame":6,"kind":null},{"id":"Q3666837","formula":"Cu₆FeSn₂S₈","names":{"en":"Chatkalite"},"elements":["S","Fe","Cu","Sn"],"fame":6,"kind":"crystal"},{"id":"Q422318","formula":"Cu₆SnMoS₈","names":{"en":"Hemusite"},"elements":["S","Cu","Mo","Sn"],"fame":6,"kind":null},{"id":"Q781943","formula":"Cu₂SnS₃","names":{"en":"Mohite"},"elements":["S","Cu","Sn"],"fame":6,"kind":"crystal"},{"id":"Q419299","formula":"Cu₂FeSnS₄","names":{"en":"Stannite","ru":"Станнин","uk":"Станін"},"elements":["S","Fe","Cu","Sn"],"fame":24,"kind":"crystal"},{"id":"Q425076","formula":"Cu₁₃Fe₂Ge₂S₁₆","names":{"en":"Germanite","ru":"Германит","uk":"Германіт"},"elements":["S","Fe","Cu","Ge"],"fame":22,"kind":"crystal"},{"id":"Q3853009","formula":"Cu₆Fe₂SnS₈","n